config:
  flowchart:
    nodeSpacing: 24
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: The way of a file from the inbox to Paperless
    accDescr: In the next run, a file in the folder Inbox is uploaded to Paperless. When Paperless is unreachable or overloaded, the file waits 15 minutes, then twice as long each time, up to a day, and is uploaded again. When Paperless refuses it, such as a file of an unsupported type, it stays in Inbox and is skipped until it is saved anew, renamed or replaced. When Paperless accepts it, the next runs follow its Paperless task while it is running: after success, the file is removed from Inbox or kept, as configured; after a failure, a duplicate or a cancelled task, it moves to the folder Failed imports, next to a .error.txt with the reason. A day after the upload, a file whose content Paperless has counts as imported; a task that Paperless still lists unfinished moves the file to Failed imports, so that a second upload can't make a duplicate; and a task that Paperless doesn't list sends the file to the wait as well, and it is uploaded again.

    %% The wait takes the uploads that failed for a time and the tasks without an end back to the upload.
    retry["Waits 15 minutes,<br>then twice as<br>long, up to a day"]
    file["📄 A file in<br>📁 Inbox"]
    upload{"Upload to<br>Paperless"}
    task{"Its task,<br>in the<br>next runs"}
    refused["Refused, such as<br>an unsupported<br>file type: stays<br>in Inbox,<br>skipped until<br>it changes"]
    done["Success:<br>removed from<br>Inbox, or kept,<br>as configured"]
    failed["Failure, duplicate,<br>cancelled, or still<br>unfinished a day<br>after the upload:<br>moved to<br>📁 Failed imports, next<br>to a .error.txt<br>with the reason"]

    retry -- "again" --> upload
    file -- "next run" --> upload
    upload -- "unreachable<br>or overloaded" --> retry
    upload -- "accepted" --> task
    upload --> refused
    refused -- "saved anew,<br>renamed or<br>replaced" --> upload
    task --> done
    task --> failed
    task -- "not listed a day<br>after the upload" --> retry

    classDef nextcloud fill:#0082c92e,stroke:#0082c9,stroke-width:2px
    classDef paperless fill:#17803d2e,stroke:#17803d,stroke-width:2px
    class file,refused,done,failed nextcloud
    class upload,task paperless
